<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RM_ScaldProtection.xml                 EnvironmentalHazards
  ==========================================================================
  SCALD_STEAM_WEATHER_DESIGN_1 step 4, built 2026-09-26. The apparel stat
  RM_HediffComp_EnvironmentalExposure reads through its own `protectionStat`
  field and sums across worn apparel (HazardTargeting.SumApparelStat — an
  "Apparel"-category StatDef has no vanilla auto-aggregation onto a pawn
  stat; the comp does the summing itself).

  Cribbed from RM_WetBulbProtection.xml in this same folder, field for
  field — that spec section says so outright ("cribbing RM_WetBulbProtection
  exactly"). Same abstract base, same 0..1 clamp, same quality part.

  ⚠️ TWO SCALD STATS, TWO JOBS, both meant to sit on the same garments —
  do not merge them and do not substitute one for the other:
    RM_ScaldProtection   — THIS one. Slows the standing-steam exposure
                           clock (RUT_ScaldExposure). Read only by the
                           exposure comp.
    RM_ArmorRating_Scald — the DAMAGE stat, for RUT_Scald hits (the steam
                           devil's vortex). Read by the armor system.
  Ordinary ArmorRating_Heat is the third, separate thing: it is what
  reduces the terrain's own wading burn, and it is plain vanilla.

  Ban 3 of the frozen sheet ("no boiling-immune traversal for free") is not
  enforced here but by the comp's own `minDriveFactor` floor: this stat is
  clamped to 1 and the clock still runs at 8% of rate at full protection.
  A garment may therefore safely carry a large value; nothing wearable
  reaches immunity.
-->
<Defs>

  <StatDef ParentName="ArmorRatingBase">
    <defName>RM_ScaldProtection</defName>
    <label>scald-steam protection</label>
    <labelForFullStatList>Scald-steam protection (armor stat)</labelForFullStatList>
    <description>How much this garment slows the scald-steam exposure clock — sealed or heavily waxed gear built to keep live steam off skin and out of lungs. Ordinary insulation does nothing against standing steam; only apparel carrying this stat helps.

Summed across every garment worn at once, then capped. Nothing reaches immunity: fully protected, the clock still runs, slowly.</description>
    <maxValue>1</maxValue>
    <parts>
      <li Class="StatPart_Quality">
        <factorAwful>0.6</factorAwful>
        <factorPoor>0.8</factorPoor>
        <factorNormal>1</factorNormal>
        <factorGood>1.15</factorGood>
        <factorExcellent>1.3</factorExcellent>
        <factorMasterwork>1.45</factorMasterwork>
        <factorLegendary>1.8</factorLegendary>
      </li>
    </parts>
  </StatDef>

</Defs>
